# callkeep: a server's later requests read as fast as its first once a pos-0 prompt call keeps its pick. Written
# 2026-11-09 on the Mac before any box run. Two binaries, one lease, the A6000: `bloomery` (main f304995c6, the tree the
# ctxplace sitting ran) and `bloomery-callkeep` (main + e27f351c1). DEPTH_SERVE_FOLD=depths, so each server answers
# D 6, 512, 4,096 in turn and every row after a server's first is [shared].
# DECOMPOSITION [derived, ~/.cache/bloomery/specs/laterreq/report.md]: main's later rows decode on the previous request's
# pool (measured folded.log: off D 4,096 shared 59.5..60.8 tg vs 67.45 first; pp 2,137..2,227 vs 2,561..2,578); with the
# fix a later request's call keeps its own pick as a first request's does: tg +11..12 %, pp +14 % on the D 4,096 shared
# rows; a D 512 row after a D 4,096 row may lose ~2 % (the better pool it inherited). First rows: identical (0 ± ruler).
kind: ab
question: on a server's later requests (fold rows [shared], D 4,096, prose ids, ctx 262,144, A6000 alone), how much faster is
  the callkeep binary than main in decode
term: tg tok/s of bloomery-callkeep against bloomery on the [shared] D 4,096 rows, the mean over the same rounds, tok/s @
  n=128, depth 4,096, ctx 262,144, --place a, MTP draft off, A6000
unit: %
predict: 6..14
rounds: 4
sd: 0.6 % AGENTS.md 「Know the ruler」 same-binary SD (the fold's shared rows scatter more: read the fold audit)
condition: depth-serve.sh under one lease on the A6000 (BLOOMERY_MODEL=qwen4exp, DEPTH_SERVE_PLACE=a, DEPTH_SERVE_CTX=262144,
  DEPTH_SERVE_N=128, DEPTH_SERVE_FOLD=depths, BLOOMERY_AB_ROUNDS=4), arms env=BLOOMERY_DRAFT=off:<tree>:<D> for both trees at
  D 6 512 4096; every lever else unset; no row [cold], [cpu-busy] or [other-busy]; no Xid and no NoRoom in any server log
decide-in: land callkeep IF its [shared] D 4,096 tg is above main's (paired lower bound > 3 %), its first rows equal main's
  within the ruler, and its [shared] rows read within 2 % of its own first rows at the same D
decide-below: the mechanism is not the whole story: read each later call's end record (kept, restored) in the server
  stderr before any other change
decide-above: more than the derivation's +14 %: main's shared rows lost more than the carried pool (read the fold audit's
  first rows of both arms for a second term) before the landing claims the number
# OUTCOME (2026-11-09, A6000, one lease, 4 rounds; ~/repo/bloomery = main f304995c6's bloomery-serve against
# ~/repo/bloomery-callkeep): DECIDE-IN. [shared] D 4,096 tg: main 60.19 / 60.49 / 60.05 (r1 r2 r4; r3 was its first row,
# 67.78), callkeep 64.97 / 67.04 / 67.22 / 66.83 -> +10.4 % on the means (r2..r4 alone 67.0, within 1.2 % of main's first
# D 4,096 row); pp 2,118..2,221 against 2,512..2,613 (+18 %). First rows (D 6): main 59.59 / 60.71, callkeep 58.93..60.57
# (within the ruler). The witness named nfsd and kswapd busy (the Spark's NFS mount) at io avg10 12; rows held steady.
# gate-gpu-qwen38-residency on the A6000: every clause green (newseq: kept true, restored 0, admitted 693); with
# .mutants/callkeep-history-ignores-pos.patch only newseq red (kept false, restored 693).
